      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Given your IT lead's concern about names and emails, stating absolutely \"no sensitive information was compromised\" is risky. It would be far safer to acknowledge the scope while maintaining confidence. You could revise the statement to say, \"We are investigating the nature of the incident, but preliminary findings suggest that while basic operational data may have been accessed, no highly sensitive financial information was impacted.\"",
